cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DTPR in research, teaching, or product disclosure, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DTPR: Digital Trust for Places & Routines"
abstract: "An open standard that explains how technology uses data, in plain language and icons. DTPR (Digital Trust for Places & Routines) is a taxonomy, a visual language and a machine-readable schema for transparently describing how devices and AI systems in places and routines collect data, make decisions, mitigate risk, and respect rights."
type: software
authors:
